{"id":"villageois","lemma":"villageois","pos":"adj","rank":4785,"glosses":["villagelike, characteristic of a village"],"ipa":"/vi.la.ʒwa/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/53/Fr-villageois.ogg/Fr-villageois.ogg.mp3","forms":{"feminine":"villageoise","masculinePlural":"villageois","femininePlural":"villageoises"},"formAudio":{"villageoise":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/LL-Q150_%28fra%29-Poslovitch-villageoise.wav"},"examples":[{"text":"Tous les villageois le connaissent.","en":"All the villagers know him.","words":[{"g":"all"},{"g":"the / them","l":"le"},null,{"g":"the / it"},{"g":"to know","l":"connaître"}]},{"text":"Les soldats ont tué de nombreux villageois.","en":"The soldiers killed many villagers.","words":[{"g":"the / them","l":"le"},{"g":"soldier","l":"soldat"},{"g":"to have","l":"avoir"},{"g":"to kill","l":"tuer"},{"g":"of / from"},{"g":"numerous, many"},null]},{"text":"Les villageois sont tous au courant de l'accident.","en":"All the villagers know of the accident.","words":[{"g":"the / them","l":"le"},null,{"g":"to be","l":"être"},{"g":"all"},null,null,{"g":"of / from"},{"g":"the / it"},{"g":"accident"}],"phrases":[[4,6,"up to date, abreast"]]},{"text":"L'explosion a terrorisé les villageois.","en":"The explosion frightened the villagers.","words":[{"g":"the / it"},{"g":"explosion"},{"g":"has","l":"avoir"},{"g":"to terrorize, terrify","l":"terroriser"},{"g":"the / them","l":"le"},null]},{"text":"Ils nous gagnèrent à eux avec leur hospitalité villageoise.","en":"They won us over with their small-town hospitality.","words":[{"g":"they"},{"g":"we / us"},{"g":"to win","l":"gagner"},{"g":"to / at"},{"g":"they","l":"ils"},{"g":"with"},{"g":"them"},{"g":"hospitality"},null]}]}